  {
   "id": 113,
   "type": "text",
   "title": "ED-269 & LARA extended properties — NOT POPULATED",
   "gridPos": {
    "h": 9,
    "w": 12,
    "x": 0,
    "y": 22
   },
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "code": {
     "language": "plaintext",
     "showLineNumbers": false,
     "showMiniMap": false
    },
    "content": "### Status: NO DATA (fields exist, values are empty)\n\nThe `uas_9.0.0` mapping defines ED-269 and LARA extended properties, but aggregating them over all 168 documents returns **zero buckets**. Verified empty:\n\n| Field | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `ed269Properties.uSpaceClass` | empty |\n| `ed269Properties.restrictionCondition` | empty |\n| `uasZone.restrictionConditions` | empty |\n| `laraAirspaceProperties.isLaraAirspace` | empty |\n| `uasZone.extendedProperties.active` | empty |\n\nNo panels are built on these fields. An empty chart here would imply *zero zones have restrictions*, which is a different and misleading claim from *this attribute is not populated in the source data*.\n\n**Action:** confirm with the data owner whether the ingest pipeline is expected to populate ED-269 extended properties. If it is, this is a data-quality defect upstream."
   },
   "pluginVersion": "12.1.1",
   "transparent": false
  },
  {
   "id": 114,
   "type": "text",
   "title": "How the map is produced",
   "gridPos": {
    "h": 9,
    "w": 12,
    "x": 12,
    "y": 22
   },
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "code": {
     "language": "plaintext",
     "showLineNumbers": false,
     "showMiniMap": false
    },
    "content": "### Geometry is derived, not read directly\n\n`uas_9.0.0` stores geometry as **`geo_shape` inside a `nested` field** (`uasZone.geometry.geom`). Grafana's Elasticsearch datasource can aggregate neither `nested` fields nor `geo_shape`, so it cannot map that index directly.\n\n`uas-zones-geo` is a **read-only derivation**: each zone's polygon is reduced to a parent-level `centroid` geo_point, which `geohash_grid` can aggregate. The source index is never modified.\n\n**Centroid method:** arithmetic mean of the exterior ring's vertices, excluding the GeoJSON closing vertex. This is a *vertex* centroid, not an area centroid — for these airspace polygons the difference is negligible and it can never fall outside the bounding box. Verified precondition: all 168 zones hold exactly one `Polygon` (168 docs : 168 nested geometry entries).\n\n**A centroid is a point, not the zone.** A large or irregular zone is drawn at its centre, so the map shows *where zones are*, not their true extent. For exact boundaries use the source geometry.\n\n**Refresh:** rebuild with `uas-zones-geo-build.sh`. The freshness row below compares counts so staleness is visible rather than silent."
   },
   "pluginVersion": "12.1.1"
  },
